BTG DAO Governance System DocumentationHere is the complete documentation and architecture overview for the BTG DAO on-chain governance system, integrated directly with your Bushido Trading Protocol.OverviewBTG DAO is the on-chain governance engine powering the BTG ecosystem. Built on smart contracts, it grants voting power based on token holdings combined with a wallet's Bushido Virtue Score—an on-chain reputation built from real trading activity and scored across eight traditional virtues.+-------------------+      +-----------------------+      +-------------------+
|  Bushido Trading  | ---> |  Virtue Audit         | ---> |   MyGovernance    |
|     Protocol      |      |     Registry          |      |  (Voting Engine)  |
|  (Swaps & Trades) |      | (Recorder Role Logs)  |      |  (+1% per 100 pts)|
+-------------------+      +-----------------------+      +-------------------+
Core Components1. BTG1 — Foundation LayerThe baseline infrastructure required for DAO operation:Treasury and fund movement (deposits/withdrawals)Access control and permission managementBase configuration updates2. BTG2 — Virtue Score FrameworkExtends BTG1 by defining the 8-virtue architecture assigned to user wallet addresses:VirtueJapaneseMeaningAcquisition MethodRighteousnessGiJustice / Doing what's rightTrading ActivityCourageYuHeroic courageTrading ActivityBenevolenceJinCompassionTrading ActivityRespectReiPolitenessNon-trade / GovernanceHonestyMakotoSincerityNon-trade / GovernanceHonourMeiyoReputation, honourTrading ActivityDutyChugiLoyaltyNon-trade / GovernanceSelf-ControlJiseiDisciplineTrading Activity3. Virtue Audit RegistryThe smart contract where virtue scores accumulate and persist on-chain:Tracks history for every token swap through the Bushido Trading Protocol.Automatically evaluates trades across 5 metrics: execution quality, conviction, liquidity depth, slippage adherence, and token transparency.Updates the running totals for Gi, Yu, Jin, Meiyo, and Jisei.4. MyGovernance — Voting EnginePowered by OpenZeppelin Governor, this contract calculates final voting weight:Voting Delay: Short holding period after proposal submission before voting begins.Voting Window: ~1 week.Proposal Threshold: 0 tokens required to submit proposals.Timelock Delay: Safety window between a passing vote and execution.How Trades Convert to Voting Power$$\text{Voting Power} = \text{Token Balance} \times \left(1 + \min\left(\frac{\text{Virtue Points}}{100} \times 0.01, \, 1.0\right)\right)$$Conversion Rate: Every 100 virtue points adds +1% extra voting weight.Cap: Voting power bonuses are capped at +100% (virtue can at most double your voting weight).Requirement: Users must hold at least 1 token to utilize a virtue bonus (virtue boosts weight; it does not generate votes without tokens).Proposal Lifecycle[ Submit Proposal ] 
